#!/bin/zsh
TMUX=/opt/homebrew/bin/tmux
[ -x "$TMUX" ] || TMUX=/usr/local/bin/tmux
$TMUX send-keys -t scribe:1.1 C-u; sleep 1
$TMUX send-keys -t scribe:1.1 "NEW TASK - BUILDER. Fix three defects in the voice enrolment write path. lx surveyed it and its evidence is at docs/handoff/scratch/lx-enrolment-survey-evidence-20-SEP-2026.md - read that first. The three, in priority order. ONE, and this is the expensive one: six of seven voiceprints KEEP NO AUDIO, so no centroid can ever be recomputed with a better model or pipeline. Enrolment is currently irreversible. Make the write path retain the enrolment audio, and say in your report what the storage cost per clinician actually is so I can judge it rather than assume it. TWO: storeEnrollmentSession at lib/voice-samples.ts:79-134 admits on ok.length < 3 - a COUNT with no minimum-duration check anywhere in the repo, so three one-second clips enrol as readily as three good ones. Add a duration floor. Do not invent the number - propose one from what the model actually needs and say what you based it on; if you cannot ground it, say so and I will rule. THREE: the inserts and recomputeCentroid are not in one transaction, so a crash between the last insert and the recompute leaves a stale centroid pointing at samples that moved. Make it atomic or make it self-healing, and say which you chose and why. CONSTRAINTS: this is the Neon HTTP driver - no sql.unsafe, no interactive transactions, timestamps come back as ISO strings. Branch from 45eedda which is production. Do NOT recompute, delete or migrate any existing centroid - seven live prints are the only voice identity we have and five of them may be our only room-domain material. Do not touch the enrolment UI. Write the tests first and prove each fix by reverting it and showing the test fails. Report: what changed, per-file, the storage number, the duration floor and its basis, atomic-or-self-healing and why, test counts, and the mutation result for each fix. Do not push. CAP 200 words."; sleep 2
$TMUX send-keys -t scribe:1.1 Enter; sleep 2
$TMUX send-keys -t scribe:1.1 Enter; sleep 1
echo sent
